          "text": "Say \"run only a recovery command documented in the CLI help, after confirming it makes no model call or that the call is within the approved budget. If the cause is an external quota or outage, record the reset time and do not clear the downgrade manually. Otherwise pause under section 17.\"",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1/claim/15",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "MINOR. The last bullet says to pause if the same acceptor is unavailable. HowlPlane's ORCHESTRATE.md allows a TAKEOVER when the orchestrator is disqualified for unrelated reasons. The bullet's \"as HowlPlane's own contract requires\" overstates that contract, though pausing is the stricter choice and is not a bypass.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1/claim/16",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "MINOR. The journal order is inconsistent. The S3b COMPLETE entry is stamped 15:15Z, before the S3 handoff (15:20Z) and the lint attempt (15:35Z). The bullet's trigger citation is therefore only loosely checkable.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1/claim/17",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1",
