  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "prompt-s18",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/2",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "r001-journal",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "BLOCKING (new permission, unsupported number) — The third-party-data bullet says \"the number of short attributed examples the user approved (R001: at most 5 per table)\". r001-journal contains no user instruction approving publication of any source records, and its 2026-10-09T04:45Z trigger says only to scan pushes and check terms. The bullet therefore creates a publication allowance that the evidence does not support. This conflicts with the prompt-s18 ban on granting new permissions. The MLBAM notice quoted in the journal (\"individual, non-commercial, non-bulk use\") is also unresolved. The \"5\" cannot be tested against a recorded approval.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Replace \"(R001: at most 5 per table)\" with \"only a number of examples the user has approved in a dated instruction recorded verbatim in the journal; if none is recorded, publish none.\"",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/5",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "BLOCKING (contradiction/untestable) — The authorization bullet says an owner authorization \"never waives third-party terms\". Its trigger (2026-10-09T09:35Z) is the case where Codex refused to fetch because the README restricted bulk use, and the fix was to state the owner's authorization verbatim. As written, a worker can still refuse after the authorization is quoted, so the lesson does not prevent the S2 failure. It also leaves unclear what an agent should do when the owner authorizes an action that terms restrict. The wording also overreaches, since the controller cannot decide whether terms are waived.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/6",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Replace the clause with \"the authorization is passed on as the owner's own decision, with its scope; it does not extend beyond the stated scope and does not authorize publication. If the restriction conflicts with the stated scope, pause under section 17.\"",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "BLOCKING (new permission, trigger does not justify it) — The Howl-repair bullet permits running an uncommitted-to-main candidate through the public CLI with PYTHONPATH pointing at a repair worktree. The cited trigger, 2026-10-08T17:45Z, is the DOG-035 review handoff and CUBS-P-002/003/004. None of those entries describes a pre-merge override run. The journal at 20:00Z verified the live engine \"without override\" only after merge. This adds a new execution path for unmerged code, which touches the isolation and runtime-state rules. The \"advisory only\" label does not remove that. \"Discard any scratch sessions it creates\" is also unscoped, so it could erase evidence and conflicts with the preserve-before-discard rule in the later bullet. Scratch sessions also consume the bounded HowlPlane session count (e.g. \"14 of 16\") and no budget treatment is stated.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Delete the PYTHONPATH sentence. If it is kept, require a dated user instruction, a session-budget count, and preservation of any discarded session's evidence.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/9",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "BLOCKING (unsupported command, possible spending or state change) — The readiness bullet names `howlplane agents doctor --live --agent <agent> --repo <repo>` as a documented recovery. r001-journal supports only `howl agents doctor` and `codex login status`. A `--live` probe may call a model, which would be spending or quota use, and it may rewrite the shared global readiness cache that the journal says persists across repos. Neither effect is addressed. \"Traced\" is also vague, since \"recorded cause is identified\" has no testable criterion.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/10",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Say \"use only a recovery command whose documentation is cited in the journal, record the command and its result, and do not run it if it would consume quota or rewrite shared state without user approval. A downgrade is traced when the journal records the failing attempt id and the error text.\"",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/11",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "minor — Several help incidents get neither a lesson nor the explicit \"no prompt change adds value\" statement that prompt-s18 requires. These are CUBS-P-003 (a planner VERIFY_COMMAND naming a nonexistent test file was cited against the work) and CUBS-P-008 (IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS: INCOMPLETE recorded as SUCCEEDED, a false-success risk). CUBS-P-004 is only partly covered by the --verify-timeout bullet.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/12",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "minor — The acceptor bullet (S3/S3b) is consistent with the quoted ORCHESTRATE.md contract. \"Recorded as findings, then satisfied within bounds or paused for\" is vague about who decides, and an acceptor could use it to add criteria after the fact. The journal timestamps are also out of order (S3b COMPLETE at 15:15Z, the lint-session attempt at 15:35Z, the S3 handoff at 15:20Z), so the cited trigger dates are uncertain.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/13",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "minor — The header says the section adds \"no authority\", and the Dream-budget and --separate bullets are consistent with that. The v1 sha256 and the \"836a839\" placement cannot be verified from the supplied evidence. The Dream formula matches the journal figures (6//2 = 3 baseline, 7 calls).",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0/claim/14",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "user_approval_of_example_count",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "prompt-s18",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/2",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "CITE",
      "text": "r001-journal",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "BLOCKING (new permission, unsupported number). Bullet 2 says the user approved \"at most 5 per table\" of short attributed examples. Nothing in r001-journal records that approval. The 04:45Z entry says only that bulk records must not be published. An invented cap would grant a new publication permission, which s18 forbids (\"Grant new permissions\") and which the bullet's own \"never infer\" rule bars.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "user_approval_of_five_examples_per_table",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/5",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Replace \"(R001: at most 5 per table)\" with \"only a number of examples the user has approved in a dated, journaled instruction; if none is journaled, the number is zero.\"",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/6",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "BLOCKING (new permission, protected state). Bullet 4 lets a controller run an unmerged, unreviewed engine candidate through the public CLI with PYTHONPATH and then \"discard any scratch sessions it creates\". No journal trigger supports this. The 17:45Z entry covers only the regression gate and the timeout. Running unmerged code on live campaign sessions is a new capability. Discarding sessions edits runtime state, which s18 protects, and it could hide consumed HowlPlane session counts (s18: \"reset consumed budgets\"). The \"advisory only\" caveat does not remove the permission.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Delete the PYTHONPATH sentence. Alternatively, limit it to a throwaway repo, state that session counts stay consumed and are recorded, and forbid discarding sessions.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "BLOCKING (weakens pause-and-help, untestable). Bullet 5 lets the controller recover readiness and continue once a downgrade \"counts as traced\". \"Identified from session or CLI evidence\" is not testable. The journal shows the campaign went to PAUSED_NEEDS_HELP on the CUBS-P-002 and CUBS-P-007 Howl failures (17:45Z, 23:35Z). The bullet turns those pauses into self-recovery, which bypasses the s17 pause-and-help rule.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/9",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Say that a Howl-caused downgrade is still recorded as a help incident and paused under section 17. Only after that may the user-approved documented recovery command be run.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/10",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "BLOCKING (unverified command, possible spending). The example `howlplane agents doctor --live --agent <agent> --repo <repo>` appears nowhere in the evidence. \"--live\" may make real agent calls that use quota or spend. That would be a spending or permission increase, and a quota-exhausted agent (CUBS-P-007) would simply fail again.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/11",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "howlplane_agents_doctor_live_semantics_and_cost",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/12",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "BLOCKING (untestable bound, possible budget evasion). Bullet 7 says to re-judge \"within the existing rework bounds\". The journal's recovery path (15:35Z) discards S3 and starts a new session. A new session restarts the \"Rework rounds: n of 2\" counter and consumes a session slot (14 of 16). So the bound cannot be checked, and the path can be used to get past an exhausted rework limit.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/13",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Add that a replacement session counts toward the session budget, that rework rounds carried over from the discarded session are recorded, and that the total rework budget is not reset.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/14",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Minor. Bullet 4's \"at least twice its last observed runtime\" gives 912 s from the observed 456 s. The journal says implementers time out at 600 s (CUBS-P-004). It is unknown whether --verify-timeout also governs those roles.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/15",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Minor. Bullet 3 embeds engine internals (the clamp formula) that will go stale. \"Verify against the engine\" is acceptable, but the formula should be marked as an example.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/16",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Minor. Bullet 6 says to discard a mission-owned session. It should say explicitly that the discard consumes no budget and that the preserved patch hash is recorded.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/17",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Minor. Bullet 1 is justified by 09:35Z. Its text \"if it is not yet in the journal, record it there\" is fine.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0/claim/18",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Minor. The 04:45Z journal entry has a stray timestamp (\"== 2026-10-09T12:37:15Z\"), so its ordering is ambiguous as a trigger.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1/claim/1",
