    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "BLOCKING (new permission, unsupported number). The bullet \"Third-party data is checked before any public push\" says \"at most 5 per table\" and calls it \"the number of short attributed examples the user approved\". The supplied journal entries contain no dated user approval of 5 examples. The 2026-10-09T04:45Z entry only records the terms incident and the lesson. Unless a dated user instruction exists elsewhere, this creates a publication allowance that section 18 says self-authored text cannot create.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Replace \"(R001: at most 5 per table)\" with \"the number the user has approved in a dated instruction recorded in the journal; if none is recorded, zero raw records\". This also fits the bullet's own default of no raw records.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1/claim/5",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "BLOCKING (new procedure and permission, not justified by its trigger). The repair bullet allows exercising a committed candidate through the public `howl` CLI with PYTHONPATH pointing at a repair worktree. The cited trigger (2026-10-08T17:45Z) concerns the narrow --verify and the 300 s timeout, not pre-merge engine overrides. The sentence adds a new execution path in which unmerged code drives live sessions. That conflicts with the bullet's own \"Never switch the shared engine checkout\" and with the claim that 19A adds no authority.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1/claim/6",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Delete the PYTHONPATH sentence. If it is kept, move it to a separately triggered, user-authorized change.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-190350-f071c0bf5d2c/candidates/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
